<title>HONG KONG: Intense quake rattles area east of Japan's Honshu.</title>
<headline>Intense quake rattles area east of Japan's Honshu.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>An intense earthquake measuring 5.8 on the open-ended Richter scale shook an area east of Japan's largest island of Honshu on Wednesday, Hong Kong's Royal Observatory said.</p>
<p>The observatory said the quake struck at 0233 GMT. The tremor was centred about 190 km (118 miles) southeast of Tokyo, it said. No further details were immediately available.</p>
